#
# H.264 for the web client.
#
# The idea of sending video while the screen is moving comes from
# KasmVNC. The encoder code does not. TigerVNC 1.16 and noVNC 1.7
# only decode encoding 50 (H264Decoder.cxx and
# core/decoders/h264.js). Nothing was copied from those decoders or
# from Kasm. H264Encoder.cxx was written for this server.
#
# The on-wire layout matches those decoders as they already are:
# encoding 50, a uint32 byte length, a uint32 flags word, then
# Annex-B. Flag bit 0 resets the decoder context for this rectangle.
#
# The behaviour around that layout is specific to this server.
# x264 is software-only, ultrafast, zerolatency, baseline, I420,
# CRF 18. One even-sized rectangle is sent while the screen is
# moving. The encoder uses one thread per CPU, up to 4. A still
# screen uses the client's normal encoders. A client that does not
# request encoding 50 keeps its own encoder.
#
